  id:'lexis', title:'Style and the argument',
  instr:'Each passage is a real one in which the style may serve the argument or take its place. We ask whether the claim still stands when it is said in plain clauses, or whether the figure is itself the claim, and what the style of the passage does for its argument. Ten questions; a passage is not repeated in the set.',
